---
import { SITE, COUNTS } from '../lib/site';
---

<footer class="foot" data-foot>
  <div class="wrap foot-top">
    <div class="foot-cta">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span class="n">{COUNTS.toGo}</span><span class="rule"></span>countries to go</p>
      <p class="foot-line">Twenty stamps left.<br />Ride along for the rest.</p>
      <a class="btn btn-gold" href={SITE.subscribe} target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-magnetic><span>Subscribe on YouTube <span class="arr">→</span></span></a>
    </div>
    <nav aria-label="Footer" class="foot-cols">
      <div>
        <p class="foot-h mono">Explore</p>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/#journey">The journey</a></li>
          <li><a href="/#globe">The globe</a></li>
          <li><a href="/countries/">All countries</a></li>
          <li><a href="/#course">Flights course</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="foot-h mono">Follow</p>
        <ul>
          <li><a href={SITE.youtube} target="_blank" rel="noopener">YouTube</a></li>
          <li><a href={SITE.instagram} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Instagram</a></li>
          <li><a href={SITE.facebook} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Facebook</a></li>
          <li><a href={SITE.graphy} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Courses on Graphy</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="foot-h mono">Contact</p>
        <ul>
          <li><a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a></li>
          <li><a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </nav>
  </div>

  <p class="wordmark" aria-hidden="true" data-wordmark>
    <span class="wm-hi" lang="hi">{SITE.nameHi}</span>
    <span class="wm-en">Yatri Doctor</span>
  </p>

  <div class="wrap foot-small">
    <p>Concept site, not affiliated with or endorsed by Navankur Chaudhary. Counts come from his public YouTube, Instagram and Graphy pages, checked on {SITE.asOfLabel}. The country map is built from his public uploads; his own count includes countries not yet in his videos.</p>
    <p>Earth imagery: NASA Visible Earth (Blue Marble, Black Marble). Country shapes: Natural Earth, India's point of view. Videos, titles, thumbnails and quotes © Yatri Doctor.</p>
  </div>
</footer>
